// SB.
//
// Store buffering: each thread stores, then loads the other thread's location,
//   and both loads see the initial value.
//
// Asserted below, by source:
//   herd7 on the zoo's cat models, run on this program: SC forbids, TSO allows,
//     Coherence allows, RC11 allows, RC17 allows, OD-LSO allows.
//   the zoo's equivalence and ordering edges:
//     VbD forbids. Equivalent to SC (zoo edge).
//     x86-TSO allows. Equivalent to TSO (zoo edge).
//     ClightTSO allows. Equivalent to TSO (zoo edge).
//     RC11z allows. Equivalent to RC11 (zoo edge).
//     MRD allows. RC11 allows it, and MRD is weaker than RC11 (zoo edge RC11 ->
//       MRD).
//     PRAM allows. PC allows it, and PRAM is weaker.
//     Slow allows. PRAM allows it, and Slow is weaker.
//     Local allows. Slow allows it, and Local is weaker.
//     RYW allows. PRAM allows it, and RYW is weaker.
//     MR allows. PRAM allows it, and MR is weaker.
//     MW allows. PRAM allows it, and MW is weaker.
//     WFR allows. Causal allows it, and WFR is weaker.
//   the models' definitions:
//     CC allows. Implied by Causal.
//     PC allows. Each location has one write, so one order per location
//       constrains nothing, and each view places the other process's write
//       last.
//     Causal allows. Each process's view can place its own write before its
//       load and the other's write after it.
//     POCausal allows. x and y are different objects, and neither read has seen
//       the write to its own location.
//   Not asserted, for want of a verdict to check against: none. RA, SRA and WRA
//     are defined on release stores and acquire loads, and this program has
//     other accesses.
x := 0;
y := 0;
{
  x := 1;
  r0 := y
} ||| {
  y := 1;
  r1 := x
}
%%
allow (r0 = 0 && r1 = 0) [TSO, x86-TSO, ClightTSO, Coherence, RC11, RC11z,
                          RC17, OD-LSO, MRD, CC, PC, PRAM, Causal, Slow, Local,
                          POCausal, RYW, MR, MW, WFR]
forbid (r0 = 0 && r1 = 0) [SC, VbD]
